# PR Draft: fix(settings): safely resolve language options and prevent crash on regional locales (#403)

Closes #403

### Summary
Fixes an issue where opening the Settings page resulted in a blank/grey box due to a crash in LanguageSelectionSetting.

### Root Cause & Fix
When a device has a regional locale set (e.g. nl_NL, en_US, de_DE), _languageOptions[settings.preferredLocaleSubtag] returned null because the map only contains base language keys (e.g. 'nl', 'de'). Using the ! bang operator caused an unhandled Null check operator used on a null value error that crashed the settings page layout.

- Replaced unsafe dictionary access with safe resolution that matches base language prefixes (e.g. nl_NL -> nl) and falls back gracefully to 'en' if unrecognized.
- Safely resolves initialValue for RadioSettingsDialog.
- Added comprehensive unit tests in language_selection_setting_test.dart.
- Verified on Android Emulator (Medium_Phone_API_37.0).
